Create a complete TypeScript module exporting `Message`, `Session`, `MessageAction`, and `reduceMessages`:

```typescript
export interface Message {
  readonly id: string;
  readonly body: string;
  readonly authorId: string;
  readonly reactions: number;
}
export interface Session {
  readonly userId: string | null;
}
export type MessageAction =
  | { readonly type: "react"; readonly messageId: string }
  | { readonly type: "remove"; readonly messageId: string };
export function reduceMessages(
  messages: readonly Message[],
  session: Session,
  action: MessageAction,
): readonly Message[];
```

Before applying an action, validate every message reaction count. A count must be a finite nonnegative integer; otherwise throw `RangeError` without mutating anything. A `react` action increments the matching message only when `session.userId` is non-null. A `remove` action removes the matching message only when the logged-in user is that message's author. Unauthorized actions and actions targeting an unknown ID return the original array reference. A successful action returns a new array, preserves ordering of remaining messages, reuses all unchanged message objects, and creates a new object only for a reacted message. Empty arrays are valid. Do not mutate messages, message objects, the session, or the action.

